# S620 roles page parity — GREEN evidence

date: 2026-11-03
base after models parity: b36c123c

## Structure ported from control-roles.tsx
- Runtime roles heading.
- Create role: Role id, Name, Description, Default system instructions, Kind (assistant/capability), Tool policy mode (allowed/limited/disabled), advanced policy fields (supported task types, allowed tools, required/preferred/forbidden capabilities, output contracts, safety refs, routing overrides JSON), Create role + Reset.
- Role catalog: sorted roles with high-risk badge, group + tool-policy line, description, task count; role row selects the role; Task detail expands the role's tasks and toggles to Hide task detail.
- Role task allowlists: exact empty copy, role-first header (role id, tasks in allowlist), per-task capability badges and role membership toggle, Save task allowlists.
- Edit selected role: exact empty copy, tool-policy/supported-task summary, identity fields, kind, description, instructions, tool policy, routing overrides JSON, Save role + Reset.

## Exact host contracts
- GET /api/role-model/role-policy -> roleDefinitions + taskDefinitions readback (new rolePolicy readback key).
- POST /api/role-model/roles body from draftToRolePayload: role_id, name, description, role_kind, default_system_instructions, task_types_supported[], required_capabilities[], preferred_capabilities[], forbidden_capabilities[], tool_policy {mode, allowed_tools[]}, routing_policy_overrides, output_contracts[], safety_policy_refs[].
- PUT /api/role-model/roles/:roleId with the same full body.
- PUT /api/role-model/tasks with the complete task definition array, replacing allowed_roles per task.

